{"id": "EUVD-2026-82094", "enisaUuid": "59dd968d-2948-31ef-b81e-22c6727520e9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nspi: oc-tiny: switch to managed controller allocation\n\nThe controller is allocated with the non-managed spi_alloc_host() while\nthe interrupt is registered with devm_request_irq().  During removal,\nspi_bitbang_stop() only unregisters the controller; the subsequent\nspi_controller_put() then frees the controller together with its\nembedded driver-private devdata, which is the IRQ handler's dev_id.  The\ndevm_request_irq() release action (free_irq()), which drains the\nhandler, does not run until after .remove() returns.  A late or latched\ninterrupt can therefore reach tiny_spi_irq() and dereference\nalready-freed memory (e.g. hw->base).\n\nSwitch to devm_spi_alloc_host() so that the devres LIFO order releases\nthe controller only after free_irq() has drained the handler, and drop\nthe now-redundant spi_controller_put() from .remove().  The probe error\npath is simplified to direct returns.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:39", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9265fa8190312b87637def1382d36fc16de3b8e8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0260c94453a08491640e61f8cf0c384edbe7bd11", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ef5cc4a8c088d05549f71950a72b5deff5000fd7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1cd16c8d68f58e54abb8f331d05469237200631f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d710f43ce30975d197f73c543bfe47b958d8ba17"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90433", "GHSA-mj54-2c5f-648c"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0579605f-8a9c-3a10-b5be-3e33de112943", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "0a290355-1e8b-33ce-b1cc-e0d5f7733a14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ce792580ea2ce6f7259b45124e9ccc4574c31606 <0260c94453a08491640e61f8cf0c384edbe7bd11"}, {"id": "1a5075c9-b9c9-33c9-b8f5-47c9c47d7b13", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ce792580ea2ce6f7259b45124e9ccc4574c31606 <ef5cc4a8c088d05549f71950a72b5deff5000fd7"}, {"id": "2402ff2f-bc8f-3abd-8b9d-ad4c816852ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ce792580ea2ce6f7259b45124e9ccc4574c31606 <d710f43ce30975d197f73c543bfe47b958d8ba17"}, {"id": "705be497-a073-3912-9039-9d567974e2b8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ce792580ea2ce6f7259b45124e9ccc4574c31606 <1cd16c8d68f58e54abb8f331d05469237200631f"}, {"id": "79ad77ab-5e90-381d-807a-f981458a96c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b00170cb-66ae-3871-bd7c-4c2cfb907508", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.39"}, {"id": "c664d499-85c7-3f52-b6f7-087e36278929", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "e4c78e4a-ad90-304c-a767-ec604453cc78", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "e4f99260-9741-3535-a428-c32453ff10b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e6f483dd-3cbe-30f8-8f52-fe474b724b25", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ce792580ea2ce6f7259b45124e9ccc4574c31606 <9265fa8190312b87637def1382d36fc16de3b8e8"}, {"id": "fd20ac5c-08d0-3758-a898-0b127aa22384", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d27d9a52-286a-3a89-a853-4d1fd299c008", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}